course: dictionary
lesson: 8366
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word round is a good example. «The first round of the quiz was hard» means one turn of a game. «A round plate» means shaped like a circle.
explain: Round can also mean on every side or in a circle. In «astronauts float because they and their station are falling round the Earth together», round means going in a circle around the Earth. Here round and around mean nearly the same thing.
explain: Round can also be a verb, as in «to round a number». To round 47 is to change it to the nearest ten, which gives 50. Ask yourself which meaning fits: a turn, a shape, a circle, or a change to a number.
fact: Round has several meanings, so always check the words around it.
fact: A round is one turn of a game, a race, a quiz or a test, as in «the first round».
fact: «A round plate» means round in shape, like a circle or a ball.
fact: «Go round the park» means on every side, or in a circle. Round and around both work here.
fact: To round 47 to the nearest ten gives 50.
exercise: «The first round of the quiz was hard.» In this sentence, what is a round? | To change a number to 50 | A plate shaped like a circle | *A turn of a game or quiz | A ball made of wood
exercise: A battery «pushes electricity round the circuit until the chemicals are used up.» What does round mean here? | *In a circle, going on every side | A turn in a quiz | Very old | A shape like a ball
exercise: To round 47 to the nearest ten gives which number? | *50 | 40 | 48 | 470
test: In «a lovely little old round red French wooden toy box», what does round describe? | Its origin | Its material | Its age | *Its shape
test: Sam plays 4 rounds with 5 points in each round. How many points does he get altogether? | *20 | 45 | 9 | 54
exam: In «In 1609-1610 Galileo's homemade telescope showed moons going round Jupiter», what does round mean? | *Going in a circle around | A shape like a ball | Changed to the nearest ten | A turn in a game
